<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edo State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edo State is a state in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, created in 1991 from the former Bendel State, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-city">Benin City</a> as its capital. It covers the heartland of the historic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Kingdom of Benin</a> and the lands of the Esan, Owan, Etsako and other peoples. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a> of Benin and the Esan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onojie">Enijie</a> remain traditional rulers in the state with ceremonial and religious authority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edo-state.jpg" alt="Edo State" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hadassah Photostorie group · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountain_hill_view,_Ososo,_Akoko-Edo-8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
